<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ratna Malla</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 1484–1520</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ratna Malla was the first king of Kantipur (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kathmandu">Kathmandu</a>), one of the three Malla kingdoms of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kathmandu-valley">Kathmandu Valley</a>. A son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yaksha-malla">Yaksha Malla</a>, he established himself at Kathmandu after his father's death and broke away from his brothers at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhaktapur">Bhaktapur</a>. He strengthened his kingdom against local nobles and neighbouring rulers and gained control of trade towards <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibet">Tibet</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ratna-malla.jpg" alt="Ratna Malla" width="320" height="318" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: anonymous · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:King_Ratna_Malla_of_Kathandu,_Nepal.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
